1
00:00:13,192 --> 00:00:14,554
Good evening, everybody.

2
00:00:14,595 --> 00:00:16,737
I trust you've had a fruitful day.

3
00:00:16,757 --> 00:00:18,158
I do not say happy.

4
00:00:18,178 --> 00:00:20,742
I'm sure it has been a happy one for you.

5
00:00:21,903 --> 00:00:37,884
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhudassa Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhudassa

6
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:46,844
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambuddhasa.

7
00:00:47,524 --> 00:00:51,673
Homage to the Buddha, the blessed, noble and fully self-awakened one.

8
00:00:54,176 --> 00:00:58,283
So we're making our way through this very rich discourse, actually.

9
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:03,432
So we'll have to just do a little quick revision on it.

10
00:01:05,471 --> 00:01:11,459
So it starts off, remember, with this ex-king, Phukasati.

11
00:01:13,361 --> 00:01:22,673
And, you know, he's from that kingdom up there, Taksila, with its famous monastery, Taksila, at Taksila, the capital.

12
00:01:23,414 --> 00:01:27,620
And it's in north of present-day Pakistan, right up there.

13
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:34,347
And it's been going since 1000 BCE, although it obviously doesn't exist anymore.

14
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:45,593
Now, the rather touching thing about this discourse is that the Buddha, one way or another, found out about Pukasati.

15
00:01:45,632 --> 00:01:53,164
Perhaps he had heard from Bimbisara that this ex-king was looking for him, was searching for him to ordain.

16
00:01:54,045 --> 00:02:02,436
Perhaps he did have this wonderful clairvoyance where he could actually contact people who were searching for him, that sort of contact.

17
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:05,921
Remember that often we will think of somebody

18
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:12,551
and we'll get a phone call from them, or we'll find something terrible has happened to them.

19
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:27,859
So there is that communication at a certain level, and somebody who's well attained, especially in concentration exercises, has that sort of power.

20
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:44,143
and uh fukusati uh is addressed by him and the and the the discourse is basically about these four things how not to neglect wisdom how to preserve the truth how to cultivate relinquishment

21
00:02:44,612 --> 00:02:45,774
and how to train in peace.

22
00:02:46,074 --> 00:02:48,758
Most of it is about this wisdom.

23
00:02:49,218 --> 00:03:11,125
And he starts off by introducing us, first of all, to the six elements, only to get us into the dependent origination, about contact, about feeling, and about the reaction to feeling, our indulgence in what is pleasant, aversion, fear to what is unpleasant, and basically an indifference to what is neutral.

24
00:03:11,564 --> 00:03:13,067
That's not even noticing it.

25
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:22,068
And within all that, there is this phrase, this is not me, it's not mine, and it's not myself.

26
00:03:23,389 --> 00:03:25,691
So there's also that understanding about it.

27
00:03:28,193 --> 00:03:33,019
And then he comes back to the six great elements.

28
00:03:33,038 --> 00:03:38,084
Remember, here we've included space and consciousness.

29
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:44,050
And finally, it is

30
00:03:46,104 --> 00:03:47,167
Where do we stop?

31
00:03:47,948 --> 00:03:48,248
Oh, yes.

32
00:03:49,151 --> 00:03:59,969
And then it was through the practice of understanding this, taking it into... Let's have a look now.

33
00:04:00,531 --> 00:04:01,954
That's right.

34
00:04:02,727 --> 00:04:30,033
taking it to the point where equanimity not indifference so now there's been a purification of the heart and we've come to equanimity and if you remember supposing a skilled goldsmith and his apprentice were to prepare a furnace heat up the crucible take some gold with tongs and put them in the crucible from time to time blow on it sprinkle water on it and just look upon it the gold will become refined well refined

35
00:04:30,014 --> 00:04:52,089
faultless rid of dross malleable wieldy and radiant and whatever kind of ornament he wished to make it would serve his purpose so too then there remains only equanimity right this wonderful state of contentment and equanimity purified bright malleable wieldy and radiant at ease with the way things are

36
00:04:54,668 --> 00:05:04,062
And so with that now, the Buddha says that he can, because this, this Bukkhasati is obviously very good at concentration.

37
00:05:04,081 --> 00:05:05,685
He sat up all night with the Buddha.

38
00:05:06,365 --> 00:05:11,293
So he says you can enter into the more refined jhanas, these

39
00:05:11,576 --> 00:05:30,740
arupa jhanas, which are basically not based on any object of mind, enter into an infinity of space, an infinity of consciousness, an infinity of nothingness, nothing is there, and even that point where there is nothing to perceive and yet there is perception.

40
00:05:32,141 --> 00:05:39,170
And because of this, he does not cling to any condition because, first of all,

41
00:05:39,742 --> 00:05:42,966
There's a danger in such things because you can be there for a very long time.

42
00:05:43,786 --> 00:05:44,987
It's still conditioned.

43
00:05:45,108 --> 00:05:47,189
It's not the end of suffering.

44
00:05:48,031 --> 00:05:56,019
And he does not form any condition or generate any volition tending towards being or non-being.

45
00:05:56,120 --> 00:06:01,026
In other words, he's let go of the idea of becoming and not becoming.

46
00:06:01,666 --> 00:06:06,112
That not becoming, of course, is getting rid of oneself.

47
00:06:06,132 --> 00:06:08,954
And he does not cling to anything in this world.

48
00:06:09,829 --> 00:06:16,057
And when he is not agitated, so he does not cling to anything in this world.

49
00:06:16,377 --> 00:06:18,839
When he does not cling, he's not agitated.

50
00:06:19,721 --> 00:06:24,927
When he is not agitated, he personally attains nirvana and he understands birth is destroyed.

51
00:06:25,668 --> 00:06:26,848
The holy life is lived.

52
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:28,992
What had to be done has been done.

53
00:06:29,331 --> 00:06:31,855
There's no more coming into a state of becoming.

54
00:06:36,221 --> 00:06:39,625
And now he goes through this pleasant feeling.

55
00:06:40,427 --> 00:06:47,555
And of course, when it comes to painful feeling, there's no indulgence with it.

56
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:55,925
When it comes to unpleasant feelings, when it comes to painful feelings, there is no holding onto it, wanting to get rid of it.

57
00:06:56,867 --> 00:07:03,035
And when it's painful, when it's neutral feeling, there's no holding, there's no intention to delight in it.

58
00:07:03,074 --> 00:07:05,858
In other words, he's found that position that we

59
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:31,625
in our practice attain when we are just observing just watching just feeling we're just aloof from the whole psychophysical organism manifesting into our awareness so he feels non-attached with these feelings and even feeling the terminating with the body when he feels

60
00:07:32,045 --> 00:07:38,012
When he feels a feeling terminating with the body, he understands a feeling terminating with the body.

61
00:07:38,052 --> 00:07:39,935
In other words, it's just in the body.

62
00:07:40,817 --> 00:07:47,807
And when he feels a feeling terminating with life, in other words, as he's approaching death, that's all he feels.

63
00:07:48,247 --> 00:07:49,569
He does not delight in it.

64
00:07:49,608 --> 00:07:50,630
He doesn't averse.

65
00:07:50,771 --> 00:07:52,213
He's not averse to it or anything.

66
00:07:52,733 --> 00:07:56,839
and he becomes quite, he becomes cool right there.

67
00:07:57,261 --> 00:08:02,990
So that's just another word to explain somebody who's fully liberated, he remains cool.

68
00:08:03,351 --> 00:08:15,012
I suppose even in the modern idiom of that's cool, you know, you're up above, aloof, and not concerned, not worried, etc.

69
00:08:17,607 --> 00:08:27,220
Just as an oil lamp burns dependent on oil and a wick, and when the oil and wick are used up, if it does not get any more fuel, it is extinguished from the lack of fuel.

70
00:08:27,761 --> 00:08:35,451
So too, when he feels a feeling terminating with the body, terminating with life, he understands that this is what is happening.

71
00:08:35,691 --> 00:08:43,902
On the dissolution of the body with the ending of life, all that is felt not being delighted in while becoming cool right there.

72
00:08:44,134 --> 00:08:55,793
So what is understood is that so long as somebody is fully liberated, remains in this life, he still has the consequences of a body, the pain of it, the death of it, etc.

73
00:08:56,335 --> 00:08:59,860
And when this drops away, then he is completely liberated.

74
00:09:02,424 --> 00:09:08,294
He's also liberated from the consequences of leftovers in his mind.

75
00:09:08,735 --> 00:09:10,698
These are called traces, vasanas.

76
00:09:11,302 --> 00:09:22,201
So there's still, you know, little bits of greed, little bits of hatred and stuff come up, but they're, as it were, just zipping through the mind.

77
00:09:22,422 --> 00:09:23,865
There's no clutching at them.

78
00:09:23,924 --> 00:09:25,447
There's no holding onto them.

79
00:09:26,269 --> 00:09:27,671
That's where the liberation is.

80
00:09:30,856 --> 00:09:36,365
And therefore the Buddha says, he has found the supreme foundation of wisdom.

81
00:09:37,611 --> 00:09:41,735
And his deliverance being founded upon this truth is unshakable.

82
00:09:42,977 --> 00:09:47,581
For that is false, which is of a deceptive nature.

83
00:09:48,543 --> 00:09:53,008
And that is true, which is of an undeceptive nature, which is Nibbāna.

84
00:09:53,227 --> 00:09:57,633
So in other words, you can't be deceived by Nibbāna.

85
00:09:57,913 --> 00:09:59,914
It doesn't deceive you.

86
00:10:01,196 --> 00:10:02,898
You can, of course, deceive yourself.

87
00:10:02,957 --> 00:10:04,399
You can think you've attained it.

88
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:07,482
But once you've actually experienced Nibbāna,

89
00:10:07,902 --> 00:10:11,346
then you can't deny it.

90
00:10:11,765 --> 00:10:28,065
It's something so different from everything else we've experienced that it remains as a truthful personal experience.

91
00:10:28,105 --> 00:10:31,107
So he possesses this supreme foundation of truth.

92
00:10:33,113 --> 00:10:36,616
Normally, when he was ignorant, he acquired and developed attachments.

93
00:10:37,118 --> 00:10:54,278
So the attachments are to the five khandhas, the psychophysical organism, to all the defilements we're attached to our little sins, to all our habits we're attached to our habits, and, of course, there's always that sensual pleasure.

94
00:10:55,899 --> 00:10:57,601
And all that has been relinquished.

95
00:10:57,869 --> 00:11:27,419
all that has gone now as a place where there's any happiness to be found and this is namely the supreme noble relinquishment when he was ignorant he experienced covetousness desire and indulgence but now he's abandoned them cut them off like uh made them like a palm stump so when you cut off the frond at the top of a palm stump that's the end of it really

96
00:11:27,754 --> 00:11:52,057
it doesn't it can't grow again so it's the same way with all the rest of the hindrances and therefore that that person possesses the supreme foundation of peace okay so this is what uh the buddha is talking to when he says don't neglect the wisdom in other words work at really trying to understand the way things are

97
00:11:52,561 --> 00:11:59,513
And that once you understood anything, actually receive it as the truth, as your personal truth.

98
00:12:00,514 --> 00:12:01,275
Hold on to it.

99
00:12:02,297 --> 00:12:09,990
And then to cultivate, continuously cultivate this letting go of what we know is actually doing us harm.

100
00:12:10,951 --> 00:12:14,518
And finally, to train that way towards peace.

101
00:12:16,168 --> 00:12:32,450
So in such a person, the tithing, the tithes of conceiving, tithes, these are the ogre, the floods, or as we had them very early on in our talks, the asada, the taints, the oozings.

102
00:12:32,470 --> 00:12:34,972
They do not sweep over such a person.

103
00:12:34,993 --> 00:12:38,498
They no longer sweep over a sage at peace.

104
00:12:38,917 --> 00:12:41,260
And all the conceiving is disappeared.

105
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:45,147
And what the Buddha means by conceiving is this, I am.

106
00:12:45,707 --> 00:12:46,369
I am this.

107
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:47,431
I shall be.

108
00:12:47,451 --> 00:12:48,852
I shall not be.

109
00:12:49,274 --> 00:12:51,277
I shall be possessed of this.

110
00:12:51,717 --> 00:12:53,000
I shall be formless.

111
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,721
I shall be precipient.

112
00:12:54,863 --> 00:12:58,649
I shall be neither precipient nor non-precipient.

113
00:12:59,068 --> 00:13:03,777
So conceiving, he says, based upon ignorance, remember,

114
00:13:04,162 --> 00:13:07,086
He's a disease, a tumor, a dart.

115
00:13:07,586 --> 00:13:12,192
By overcoming all these conceivings, the sage is at peace.

116
00:13:13,293 --> 00:13:18,419
The sage at peace is not born, does not age, does not die.

117
00:13:19,221 --> 00:13:21,984
He's not shaken and does not yearn.

118
00:13:22,644 --> 00:13:26,229
For there's nothing present in him by which he might be born.

119
00:13:27,350 --> 00:13:29,594
Not being born, how could he age?

120
00:13:30,455 --> 00:13:32,397
Not aging, how could he die?

121
00:13:32,865 --> 00:13:35,188
not dying, how could he be shaken?

122
00:13:35,288 --> 00:13:36,350
How could he be fearful?

123
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:40,173
Not being shaken, how could he yearn for anything?

124
00:13:41,575 --> 00:13:44,317
So this is the Arahant, you see, fully liberated.

125
00:13:47,241 --> 00:13:54,629
Now, at this point, Phukasati suddenly realizes that perhaps this is the Buddha.

126
00:13:55,129 --> 00:14:00,696
Now, the conversation here is a bit difficult to accept, but we'll go through it anyway.

127
00:14:01,232 --> 00:14:07,261
he suddenly realizes that in fact this is the Buddha, the sublime one, the fully enlightened one.

128
00:14:07,282 --> 00:14:13,471
And he rose and arranged his upper robe over his shoulder and bowed to the Buddha.

129
00:14:13,971 --> 00:14:22,465
A transgression overcame me in that like a fool, confused and blundering, I presumed to address the blessed one as friend.

130
00:14:23,105 --> 00:14:30,496
So in the order you address somebody below you as abuso, friend, and they address you as bantei.

131
00:14:31,371 --> 00:15:00,500
uh which means uh um venerable uh reverend of course i i personally prefer adorable yes um and and uh surely uh surely because it says the border a transgression overcame you in that like a fool confused and blundering you presume to address me as a friend but since your your transgression as such

132
00:15:01,038 --> 00:15:07,264
But since you see your transgression as such and make amends in accordance with the Dhamma, we forgive you.

133
00:15:08,004 --> 00:15:20,456
For it is growth in the noble one's discipline when one sees one's transgression as such, makes amends in accordance with the Dhamma and undertakes to restrain in the future.

134
00:15:20,937 --> 00:15:22,979
Now, that all seems a little bit tough, doesn't it?

135
00:15:22,999 --> 00:15:28,884
Because, you know, it's not as though he knew the Buddha and then addressed him wrongly.

136
00:15:29,184 --> 00:15:30,506
He didn't know at all.

137
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:32,370
So it's hardly blameable.

138
00:15:32,951 --> 00:15:39,721
And I think what happened originally, probably, is that he suddenly realized and asked, are you the good?

139
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:41,082
Are you the blessed one?

140
00:15:41,102 --> 00:15:42,504
Are you Gautama?

141
00:15:43,145 --> 00:15:46,191
And when he said yes, he was sort of taken aback, you see.

142
00:15:46,871 --> 00:15:47,852
And he said, oh, I'm sorry.

143
00:15:47,913 --> 00:15:49,254
I'm sorry for aggressing you.

144
00:15:49,274 --> 00:15:49,875
I said, no.

145
00:15:50,155 --> 00:15:54,383
The Buddha said, no, no worries, no problem.

146
00:15:54,403 --> 00:15:56,525
I'm reminded of an occasion when...

147
00:15:56,927 --> 00:16:01,974
a young boy for some reason needed cheering.

148
00:16:01,994 --> 00:16:12,225
I can't remember what the reasons were, but what they thought they would do was invite David Beckham to come because he was the boy's big hero.

149
00:16:12,745 --> 00:16:15,509
Now, when David Beckham turned up, this boy couldn't handle it.

150
00:16:15,548 --> 00:16:18,732
He suddenly burst into tears and everybody had to give him a hug.

151
00:16:19,927 --> 00:16:30,386
So it might have been like this with Bukkha Sati when he suddenly realizes the person in front of it is the person whom he has taken refuge in, in his heart.

152
00:16:30,888 --> 00:16:33,513
And now, of course, he wants to take the full ordination.

153
00:16:34,533 --> 00:16:37,779
So the Buddha says to him, are your bowl and robes complete?

154
00:16:37,941 --> 00:16:41,246
Now, when you get ordained, you need these requisites.

155
00:16:41,267 --> 00:16:43,370
You need your three robes.

156
00:16:43,390 --> 00:16:44,231
You need a belt.

157
00:16:45,899 --> 00:16:52,750
You need your arms bowed, you need a razor for shaving, a needle for mending your clothes and a water strainer.

158
00:16:53,390 --> 00:16:59,639
If you take water in the wild, you're supposed to strain it just in case you don't swallow creatures.

159
00:17:00,881 --> 00:17:04,268
So he said, no, he said, I've not got them complete.

160
00:17:04,327 --> 00:17:09,695
So he says, I cannot give you full ordination until you've got your requisites complete.

161
00:17:10,132 --> 00:17:36,544
anyway pukasati having delighted and rejoiced in the blessed one word blessed one's words rose from his seat and after paying homage to the blessed one keeping him on his right he departed in search of bowl robes and requisites and while the venerable pukasati was searching for a bowl and robes a stray cow killed him hey what a bit of that well it's not such a bad luck because

162
00:17:37,839 --> 00:17:45,111
As we see now, later on, a number of monks went to the Blessed One and paying homage, etc.

163
00:17:47,032 --> 00:17:53,742
They asked, after your brief instruction to him, he died, what is his destination?

164
00:17:54,324 --> 00:17:56,247
What is his future course?

165
00:17:57,367 --> 00:18:01,974
And the Buddha replies, ah, the clansman Pukkasati was wise.

166
00:18:02,208 --> 00:18:08,878
He practiced in accordance with the Dharma and did not trouble me with interpretation of the Dharma.

167
00:18:09,118 --> 00:18:10,361
In other words, didn't argue with him.

168
00:18:12,124 --> 00:18:16,191
Obviously, people love to get into a discussion and even argument with the Buddha.

169
00:18:17,092 --> 00:18:27,067
With the destruction of the five lower fetters, right there while he was talking to him, the Klansman Phukasati has reappeared spontaneously in the pure abodes.

170
00:18:27,807 --> 00:18:33,599
So that's the place you go to when you are a non-returner.

171
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:36,105
You're not going to come back here as a human being.

172
00:18:36,646 --> 00:18:41,057
And he will attain final Nibbana there without returning to this world.

173
00:18:42,573 --> 00:18:44,515
That is what the Blessed One said.

174
00:18:44,535 --> 00:18:48,538
The bhikkhus were satisfied and delighted in the Blessed One's words.

175
00:18:49,078 --> 00:18:51,801
So here we have, I think, is a rather touching story.

176
00:18:52,001 --> 00:18:54,365
It's a bit unfortunate he got killed by a cow.

177
00:18:54,625 --> 00:18:59,349
He's not the only one in the scriptures who gets killed by cows.

178
00:18:59,410 --> 00:19:01,872
So they must have been pretty fierce in those days.

179
00:19:01,892 --> 00:19:04,654
That's the only way I can understand it, really.

180
00:19:06,257 --> 00:19:09,660
So there we have Pukasati, just in a long discourse,

181
00:19:10,348 --> 00:19:14,214
becoming a full, a non-returner.

182
00:19:14,496 --> 00:19:15,517
So that gives us hope.

183
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:28,678
So I hope you found this discourse encouraging and that you will continue with your practice until you are fully liberated sooner rather than later.

